# Spark DS — Icons

## Source

Use icons from `assets/icons/` when a match exists. Each icon has two SVG files in kebab-case:

- `{name}-medium.svg` (24×24 viewBox, 24px)
- `{name}-small.svg` (16×16 viewBox, 16px)

Examples: `search-medium.svg`, `search-small.svg`, `chevron-left-large-medium.svg`, `category-plus-medium.svg`.

Regenerate the folder from Figma with:

```bash
python3 scripts/export_figma_icons.py --from-repo-batches
```

Set `FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN` (or `~/.figma_access_token`) for a full REST export from Icons Outlined (`984:12`). Without a token, the script merges cached batches under `scripts/.icon_batches/`.

## Size tokens

| Variant | File suffix | Button token | Dimensions |
|---------|-------------|--------------|------------|
| Medium | `-medium.svg` | `--semantic-button-icon-size-medium` | 24px |
| Small | `-small.svg` | `--semantic-button-icon-size-small` | 16px |

Pick the variant that matches the component size. Do not scale a Small SVG to Medium dimensions in CSS.

## Naming

Figma frame names map to kebab-case file stems:

1. Strip trailing ` Icons`, then trailing ` Icon`
2. Replace ` + ` with `-plus-`
3. Lowercase, spaces and punctuation become hyphens

| Figma frame | Files |
|-------------|-------|
| Search Icon | `search-medium.svg`, `search-small.svg` |
| Chevron left large Icon | `chevron-left-large-medium.svg`, `chevron-left-large-small.svg` |
| Category + Icons | `category-plus-medium.svg`, `category-plus-small.svg` |

## Implementation

- Import the size you need: `import SearchMedium from 'assets/icons/search-medium.svg'`.
- Prefer inline SVG React components or imports from a shared icons module in your app.
- In React, override `fill` with `currentColor` (or `stroke="currentColor"`) so icons inherit token-driven text color. Exported SVGs use `fill="black"` as the Figma source default.
- Size icons with component tokens (e.g. `--semantic-button-icon-size-medium`), not fixed px in JSX.
- Pass `aria-hidden="true"` when the icon is decorative; the parent control must expose an accessible name.

## Button icons

- Leading icon: place icon before label in DOM (default).
- Trailing icon: keep icon before label in DOM; add `spark-btn-icon-end` class.
- Icon-only: add `spark-btn-icon-only` and required `aria-label`.

```tsx
<button type="button" className={cn('spark-btn', 'spark-btn-primary', 'spark-btn-medium', iconEnd && 'spark-btn-icon-end')}>
  <PlusIcon aria-hidden="true" />
  Add item
</button>
```

## Do not

- Import icon libraries (Lucide, Heroicons, Font Awesome) unless the project already standardizes on one **and** Spark has no equivalent.
- Use emoji or bitmap images for UI icons in product code.
- Reference undocumented icon names; browse `assets/icons/` or the Figma Icons Outlined section for available sets.
